<metadata><name>Lower Twin Lake (from Frog Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:173-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.229008" lon="-121.699244"><ele>1195.6</ele><name>Frog Lake Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:frog-lake-sno-park (OSM way 39508682); confidence: high; pdf_page: 175; quote: Locate the Pacific Crest Trail (PCT) at the north end of Frog Lake Sno-Park, then follow it as it winds gently upward through old-growth forest then through second growth.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.237041" lon="-121.686448"><ele>1340.3</ele><name>PCT / Lower Twin Lake Trail junction</name><desc>source: OSM node 985022356, south end of Twin Lakes Trail #495 on the PCT (as 172-2); confidence: high; pdf_page: 175; quote: At 1.5 miles a side trail to Lower Twin Lake leaves the PCT at a right angle, climbing gently eastward for 100 yards to a pass at 4,460 feet.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.239891" lon="-121.677555"><ele>1293.0</ele><name>Near Lower Twin Lake (north shore)</name><desc>source: OSM node 495566526 on Twin Lakes Trail #495 where side path way 73150930 leaves toward the lake (as 172-2); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 175; quote: From the pass make a long, gentle traverse downward, then turn sharply right and ski 150 yards to a point near the north shore of the lake.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.239519" lon="-121.678152"><ele>1282.3</ele><name>Lower Twin Lake shore</name><desc>source: OSM node 867738264, end of side path way 73150930 at the lake; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 175; book_elev_ft: 4160; quote: Leave the trail and descend an easy, short, but steep slope to the lake.</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Lower Twin Lake (from Frog Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>1. Frog Lake Sno-Park -&gt; PCT / Lower Twin Lake Trail junction: osm (high), 1.39 mi | 2. PCT / Lower Twin Lake Trail junction -&gt; Near Lower Twin Lake (north shore): osm (high), 0.67 mi | 3. Near Lower Twin Lake (north shore) -&gt; Lower Twin Lake shore: osm (medium), 0.04 mi</desc>
